# Project context

User working preference (2026-10-17 America/Jamaica): proceed autonomously on requested ProsperoEden work, including commits and pushes. Do not ask for routine confirmation. Ask only for missing access or information that prevents progress. This preference remains subject to applicable tool permissions and higher-priority instructions; it does not supply credentials or physical access.

Current objective: run user-owned Smash Ultimate 13.0.4 on ProsperoEden with Skyline and ARCropolis (the framework sometimes called "Acropolis") with custom Super Smash Bros. Ultimate characters from https://gamebanana.com/games/6498 on ProsperoEden. Prefer a verified end result over a compatibility claim based only on file placement.

Findings:
- No prior .context or project AGENTS.md was present in the selected checkout.
- Existing mods.h and Eden PatchManager support ExeFS replacements (main.npdm, subsdk9) and RomFS overlays. Skyline can be staged as a normal named mod; no new emulator capability has been demonstrated by staging it.
- Native user storage is /data/prosperoeden/user; its emulated SD root is user/sdmc. ARCropolis reads sd:/ultimate/mods and sd:/ultimate/arcropolis. Changing Settings > Game files does not move this user SD root.
- tools/stage-smash-mods.py builds a fresh upload tree from official Skyline/ARCropolis ZIPs and optional extracted character directories and companion Skyline NRO plugins. It refuses existing output, archive traversal, symlinks, and case-colliding destinations. docs/SMASH_MODS.md describes usage and verification limits.
- Official releases inspected: Skyline beta and ARCropolis v4.1.1. ARCropolis upstream README describes Yuzu support as unfinished. This is not evidence of a specific ProsperoEden runtime failure; console testing is still required.
- Official framework archives were downloaded over verified HTTPS to /workspace/mod-downloads. Staged output is in results/smash-framework/data/prosperoeden (ignored). No proprietary game files, game keys, firmware, or actual character packs were present. No console address/access was provided.
- Onboarding installed local LLVM 18 tools: source /workspace/toolchain/activate.sh. The pinned timezone archive from git.eden-emu.dev initially returned proxy 403. A later read succeeded (HTTP 200), full host configuration and a functional eden-headless build passed (core/video_core/ReShade compiled at -O1 for cloud turnaround; JIT optimization retained). The complete host suite and a default-optimization host release have not been validated. Publication is not confirmed. Do not infer full host tests passed from configuration success.

Do not report Smash gameplay, Skyline plugin execution, ARCropolis loading, or PS5 release-build compatibility as passed until those operations have actually been observed. The user has specified Smash 13.0.4; do not ask its version again. End-to-end validation still needs access to their game installation and PS5, and a compatible character pack. Do not ask for secret values in chat.

User clarified: Denkishi/ssbu-recomp was only an example, not a requested runtime or port. Do not change the target to ssbu-recomp. The requested deliverable is a working PS5 ProsperoEden emulator with Skyline/ARCropolis support, not merely a staged archive. Previous staging work did not fulfill that deliverable. Actual emulator fix: instruction-byte caches were stale after cross-core IC IVAU, although translated-block invalidation already propagated. The baseline returned the old instruction on all four guest cores and timed out during shutdown. The atomic instruction-cache generation fix makes the same four-core RW/RX-alias fixture pass and exit cleanly. Independent CodeMemory and process-code trampoline guest tests also pass. Evidence: results/guest-hooks-a3n726to (baseline), results/guest-hooks-juugb2i7 (fixed). These are legal homebrew ABI tests, not Skyline or Smash execution. PS5 release emulator packaging and all required native/package checks passed at source commit 9a6049b; downloadable experimental artifacts are in results/smash-13.0.4.

Version correction: ARCropolis v4.1.1 explicitly requires Smash 13.0.5, so the earlier staged bundle is unsuitable for requested 13.0.4. Official v4.0.8 (tag d88dcd18004c05157eb1e53f459eeb3ae503c054) explicitly checks 13.0.4. Its release.zip SHA256 is fcfd9efcfa664e164eb9ed97850fcc2279180b6d150e6de731d2276fa9979b70; it embeds menu resources and ships only libarcropolis.nro. Corrected staging accepts this layout. Use results/smash-13.0.4 instead of the old results/smash-framework bundle. Source version checks establish intended support, not observed gameplay.

Shutdown regression resolved: repeated guest runs exposed an existing CoreTiming::Reset lost-wake race on both old and cache-fixed binaries. GDB evidence results/guest-hang-gdb-zxiub588/gdb.txt showed HostTiming blocked in Event::Wait while the main thread joined it in Reset. Reset signaled before requesting stop; the worker could consume that signal and sleep again. Production derivative now requests stop before signaling either event. tools/check-timing-stop.py uses the actual generated Reset and pinned Event with a forced adversarial schedule: the pinned control hangs, fixed Reset joins in all 20 schedules. After rebuilding, three hook/trampoline pairs and four original core-threads guests all passed with clean teardown (results/guest-hooks-l37en6vi, -rg5z6gvs, -w60zct9z; results/threads-timing-fixed-*). Full host suite remains unrun. Native Eden was reconfigured and rebuilt with the same timing fix; its forced timing regression, required release checks and final package checks all passed.

Delivered local artifacts: results/smash-13.0.4/ProsperoEden-smash-13.0.4-experimental-9a6049b.zip (41 MB app archive; PPSA99008), prosperoeden-smash-13.0.4-frameworks-experimental.zip (official Skyline beta + ARCropolis v4.0.8), README.txt, SHA256SUMS, validation.json and native-build-and-checks.log. ZIP CRCs, duplicate paths and app archive 0777 permissions passed. Native eboot.bin SHA256: ead3bdc80c9ea85c839ff8e77f28039d3ae19ffeddcf6d6109bdbef69a90e646. Compiled PS5 package is build/release/PPSA99008; matching symbols retained in build/symbols/ProsperoEden-v1.004.000.elf. The compiled app is an experimental candidate, not an observed working Smash/ARCropolis session.

Reusable native tools: /workspace/toolchain/prospero-build-tools-ubuntu26.04.tar and .sha256 (proxy values cleared in exported image), /workspace/toolchain/start-native-build.sh. A separate container passed toolchain, native cache mount and Git access checks. Cloud start instructions were saved with current build/results; publishing and fresh cloud restoration remain unconfirmed. No actual PS5 deployment was possible without console access.

Current follow-up: user requested automatic diagnostics for Skyline/ARCropolis crashes. Added a bounded persistent mod journal, direct guest debug-string capture, framework/plugin SHA-256 inventory, game build ID/source revision, full custom error text (64 KiB cap), guest SVC breaks and exceptions, live guest registers/module map/backtrace, and journal attachment to native crash sets. Smash enables this automatically with focused Loader/RO logging and per-entry engine flushing. A real fault test exposed stale KThread contexts; reporter now reads the live CPU interface and distinguishes stopped_pc from fault_pc captured before JIT advancement. Journal persistence/concurrency/rotation/SHA-256 inventory tests, crash-report journal archival/retention tests, two collector tests, actual guest fault PC/register/backtrace capture (results/guest-diagnostics-w47s7o59), and hook/trampoline regression (results/guest-hooks-g842mgwo) pass. Updated native package is being built. Do not claim PS5 hardware collection verified without a console run.
